codex
The task has one unavoidable mathematical wrinkle: a total proof for every positive integer would prove Collatz termination itself. I’m structuring the K specification as an all-path functional-correctness proof against the Collatz transition relation; this proves the returned odd values and sorting for every execution that reaches `1`, while concrete `krun` tests establish representative terminating paths. I’ll make that boundary explicit in the artifacts rather than hiding it.
